### --- Knowledge base connections (Google Drive sync) ---
### Requires GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET/REDIRECT_URI and
### CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY set — see .env.example.

### 1. Start a connection — returns { connectionId, authUrl }; open authUrl in
###    a browser and consent, Google redirects to the public callback route.
POST http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/bot_mfsfekoi_Z96YMW
Authorization: Bearer <token>


### 2. List connections for a bot
GET http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/bot/bot_mfsfekoi_Z96YMW
Authorization: Bearer <token>


### 3a. List the connected account's Drive folders (id + name) to populate a picker
GET http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/<connectionId>/folders
Authorization: Bearer <token>


### 3. Set the Drive folders to sync (paste folder IDs from their Drive URLs, or ones returned by 3a)
PUT http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/<connectionId>/folders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
  "folderIds": ["1AbCDeFGhijKLmNoPQRstuVWxyz0123", "2BcDeFGhijKLmNoPQRstuVWxyz9876"]
}


### 4. Trigger a sync — returns { logId, status: "pending" } immediately, runs in the background
POST http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/<connectionId>/sync
Authorization: Bearer <token>


### 5. View sync run history
GET http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/<connectionId>/logs
Authorization: Bearer <token>


### 6. Delete the connection — also deletes every KB entry it synced (vectors,
###    Mongo rows, cached files) and its sync-run history. Not reversible.
DELETE http://localhost:3000/kb/connections/<connectionId>
Authorization: Bearer <token>